      case_discussion = $disc3$Cr 0.9 vs. baseline 0.3 is a 3x rise -> KDIGO Stage 3. BUN/Cr ratio = 42/0.9 ≈ 47 (>20), concentrated urine (SG 1.028), and a low urine sodium all support a prerenal cause from GI volume losses — an isotonic fluid bolus with reassessment of urine output and creatinine trend is the appropriate first step. Failure of creatinine to improve with adequate volume repletion, or a falling FeNa/BUN-Cr pattern that doesn't correct, should prompt reconsidering an intrinsic process instead.$disc3$
